# The opening's fourth beat (#230): swept through the fog into the Grave of
# the Lanterns, the pull, and the rescue in the deep. Played by IntoTheGrave
# (scripts/intro/into_the_grave.gd, scenes/prototype/intro/into_the_grave.tscn).
# Placeholder writing: rewrite freely.
#
# There are two parts, each its own conversation the scene starts:
# - start runs while you drift over the Grave, rowing taken from you.
#   You can turn the camera while it plays. It ends on the ringing; then the
#   scene takes him off the pole itself, and offers "Reach for him".
# - the_rescue is the rescue as built in intro.dlg (#183), with the same
#   pictures (scenes/prototype/intro/underwater.tscn), but his lines are for
#   a friend: you went in after him, and in the deep, spent from the Grave's
#   pull, he still finds you and gives you nearly all his light. (intro.dlg
#   still has the stranger's version, for the old opening, until this beat is
#   joined to the chain breaking, #229, and the ship finding you, #231.)
#
# Looks: bow_lantern is the lantern on the rowboat's pole, sinking_lantern is
# the one in the water. His looks are listed in scripts/companion/lantern_face.gd.

# Lights below, coming up. He's thrilled: he thinks it's home.
~ start
@look bow_lantern pleased
@wait 1.5
lantern: There you are...
@wait 0.6
lantern: Look! Lights, all the way down.
lantern: I knew there'd be somewhere. I knew it.
-> the_dead

# The nearest lights are cold. The camera looks down at them (the Grave's own
# set, scenes/prototype/intro/grave.tscn, its clips over_the_grave and
# that_one): dead lanterns, thousands of them, caught in great chains. He says
# what they are, short and stunned, and doesn't explain. Then, from far below,
# the ringing.
~ the_dead
@look bow_lantern surprised
@stage grave
@play over_the_grave
lantern: Wait...
@play that_one
@look bow_lantern worried
lantern: These are... they're lanterns.
lantern: Like me. They're all...
@wait 1.6
@stage off
@wait 1.0
lantern: ...Oh.
@wait 0.8
@sound ring
@wait 1.6
lantern: That sound. Do you hear it?
@look bow_lantern pleading

# The dark. The water closes over, and a long way above, a bell: the first
# thing that isn't the Grave. (The screen is black from the capsize.)
~ the_rescue
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@sound bell
@fade in 1.0
-> light

# A small warm thing comes through the surface, a long way off, and drives
# down through the dark to you. It's dimmer than it was: the Grave has had a
# lot of it already. His light finds dim shapes hanging all round: lanterns.
~ light
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern determined
@look sinking_lantern clear
@look sinking_lantern mended
@play lantern_appears
@play lantern_drives
@look sinking_lantern tired
@play lantern_arrives
-> finds_you

# He dips to look for a response. You don't answer.
~ finds_you
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern surprised
lantern: You came in after me?
@look sinking_lantern worried
lantern: You can't swim in this. Nobody can.
@play searches_your_face
lantern: Oh, don't go quiet on me. Not you.
-> tries

# He gets under you and heaves, and you go on sinking: there's too little of
# him left to lift you. He looks up at the surface, so far above, and back at
# you.
~ tries
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern effort
@say_in 1.2 lantern 2.4 Come on. Come on!
@play heaves
@look sinking_lantern worried
@play looks_up
@look sinking_lantern determined
lantern: Hold on. I've still got something.
-> reach

# A flame can't reach through glass, so he opens his own door and his flame
# comes out into the shape of a hand, and holds it out to you. It waits for as
# long as it takes. You can take it at any moment.
~ reach
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern effort
@play opens_door
@look sinking_lantern determined
@start reaches_out
@queue offered
@say_in 1.6 lantern 2.6 Here. Take my hand.
@wait_for interact Take his hand
@sound grasp
@look sinking_lantern calm
@play taken
-> it_catches

# The touch. A strange note through the water. He freezes, and his flame
# flares brighter.
~ it_catches
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern surprised
@play catches
lantern: Oh...
-> it_flows

# The light runs out of his hand into yours, along your arm, and you begin to
# glow. And a thinner thread of it sinks away from him, down to the dead
# lanterns far below (the Drain node): they're drawing on him too, and have
# been since the pole. He tries to pull away, and it holds, and his flame
# shrinks (#203).
~ it_flows
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern worried
@play flows
lantern: The lanterns down there...
lantern: they've been calling my light since the pole.
@look sinking_lantern effort
@play pulls_back
@look sinking_lantern pleading
lantern: I can't...
lantern: I can't hold on to it.
-> the_deep_stirs

# All round, the dead lanterns flicker. A deep rumble. He looks down:
# something enormous shifts in the dark below, passing beneath the chains,
# shown only in the lightning.
~ the_deep_stirs
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern surprised
@start stirs
@wait 1.4
@hush on
@sound deep_note
@wait 1.6
@lightning
@wait 2.2
@lightning
@wait 2.8
@hush off
-> lets_go

# He looks back at you, almost out. He chooses, and lets the last of it go:
# a burst of gold that fills everything. White. Silence. The scene ends here,
# on the white: what comes next is the ship finding you (#231).
~ lets_go
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern tired
@play looks_back
lantern: You came in after me.
lantern: So I'm not letting go of you, either.
@look sinking_lantern determined
@start lets_go
@wait 1.2
@hush on
@fade white 1.2
@stage off
@muffle off
@wait 2.5
